\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"34b671fb02318b2c8a5c81fd760d3f7b84029b0ffacf94053553b0ede8e08ac4","event_uuid":"7a89371b-eee6-4909-b02b-f8c79f6c64fb","position":{"commit_sha":"a846aedae0e3ff86b3cba4437b2dc009be10af74","position":"1787557367388766001-7a89371b-eee6-4909-b02b-f8c79f6c64fb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d8af8c17c4bddd18db3e4afaca65b217201aaba9eaaefa691827cfe8bb66a5aa","event_uuid":"7ed755b1-fc42-4109-b2a9-f5b7daebe4fc","position":{"commit_sha":"4fdae866056d4597581b5d699f938737f5b09b1f","position":"1787557899056617001-7ed755b1-fc42-4109-b2a9-f5b7daebe4fc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"930a09fd68ac52875484393a5acd5574bdb491fb6240e1f91f2f072893aaa9ce","event_uuid":"8ea93ebb-095b-4cc4-88fa-c11825ca4fe9","position":{"commit_sha":"4ced9d179c1c8ef159d013992ae10f843e8bcc3a","position":"1787557921674853001-8ea93ebb-095b-4cc4-88fa-c11825ca4fe9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"af1c63ef2e0291b7f40183611c2c48d96b496ed0fbfbfc43dc53868a90d84b0a","event_uuid":"8dbf8ff5-320d-4c1d-a81d-74221d438763","position":{"commit_sha":"fceaa32971737e1daa19fbd9b907ac2536e49110","position":"1787557956133454001-8dbf8ff5-320d-4c1d-a81d-74221d438763"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"82fa901fc17310a7c5d7e1f93919ede77349d213dd999258f9e8344d5ab42186","event_uuid":"fa129565-b1c7-490d-ab1e-8f4086d7d9c7","position":{"commit_sha":"39b59e5d7087d11a78d7e5aa5770b94bff157158","position":"1787558028124145001-fa129565-b1c7-490d-ab1e-8f4086d7d9c7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## ROOT CAUSE — PROVEN (transient runner-FS INDEX-write fault, self-heal coverage gap)\n\nThe production `rebar create` write surfaced `fatal: unable to write new index file` because\nthat signature is the ONE member of git's runner-FS transient WRITE family that the store's\nshared self-heal does not cover.\n\n### Mechanism (cited to git + the store seam)\n- `stage_and_commit` (`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py`) runs `_git_add` then `_git_commit`\n  (`src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py`). Both compose the shared retries\n  `_with_index_lock_retry` (OUTER, index.lock contention + stale reclaim) around\n  `_with_transient_fault_retry` (INNER, runner-FS transient faults).\n- The INNER retry fires only on `git_outcome.TRANSIENT_WRITE_MARKERS`\n  (`src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py`): `unable to create temporary file`,\n  `failed to insert into database`, `unable to index file`. All three are the object-DB\n  loose-object temp-create member of the family.\n- `fatal: unable to write new index file` is git's lockfile-commit failure for the INDEX\n  write (`read-cache.c` `write_locked_index`/`do_write_index` via `commit_lock_file`),\n  emitted by `git add` / `git write-tree` / a commit's pre-ref-update index prep. Confirmed\n  present verbatim in this host's git binary string catalog (`/opt/homebrew/bin/git`).\n- It matches NONE of the transient markers today (verified at runtime):\n  `is_transient_object_write(\"...unable to write new index file\")` -> False,\n  `is_index_lock` -> False, `is_git_lock` -> False, `is_invalid_object` -> False. So it is\n  returned on the FIRST attempt as a hard `StoreError` and surfaces to the caller — exactly\n  the reported \"operator retry required\".\n- The transient fingerprint matches the report: 458 GiB free, ample inodes, clean status\n  afterward, no `index.lock`, and an identical retried create succeeded — a filesystem hiccup\n  on the index write, not a data fault or lock contention.\n\n### Idempotency / safety of the retry (AC: recovery commits exactly one intended event)\ngit has a SEPARATE, distinct message for a POST-ref-update index-write failure:\n`repository has been updated, but unable to write` + `new_index file.` (underscore). That\nstring does NOT contain the contiguous substring `unable to write new index file`, so the\nmarker cannot match it (verified: `is_transient_object_write(post_ref_msg)` -> False).\nTherefore a match provably means git had NOT yet moved HEAD — no commit landed — so re-running\n`git add`/`git commit` cannot duplicate or omit an event. This is consistent with the\nproduction evidence that an exact-title search found NO created ticket (the failed write left\nnothing committed). Under the exclusive write lock the retry also cannot overwrite a concurrent\nticket write.\n\n### Reconciliation with lowcost-unsainted-wallaby (50b1)\nThat ticket correctly kept this string OUT of the index-lock CONTENTION classifier\n(`_is_git_lock_error`), because in its TEST the message came from the test's own timer deleting\ngit's real `index.lock` (force-reclaiming it would have masked a test bug). That reasoning is\nabout the lock/force-reclaim path and is unchanged here. This fix adds the string to the\nrunner-FS transient WRITE family instead — a bounded backoff RE-RUN with NO reclaim — which is\nthe mechanism the sibling object-DB faults already use. The two paths do not overlap.\n\n### Origin (caused_by)\nThe transient-write marker table was introduced by edf7-946e-84be-48b3 (\"retry transient git\nobject-DB failure on `git add`\") covering only the object-DB temp-create signatures; the\nsibling index-write signature was omitted from that family at creation, and stayed omitted when\nthe table was consolidated into `git_outcome` (unheedful-custodial-bluebottle) and extended to\n`git commit` (interior-raspberry-titi). This bug is the residual of that coverage gap.","timestamp":1787552153028566001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED: Gerrit change 2176 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2176) merged to main as df8582f6e53c with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. Fix: added 'unable to write new index file' to git_outcome.TRANSIENT_WRITE_MARKERS so the shared _with_transient_fault_retry self-heals the transient INDEX-write fault on git add/commit. Closed regression, caused_by edf7-946e-84be-48b3.","timestamp":1787558028124145001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787516356549067001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"155143cf-5a63-40fb-b0a8-dec3e7d7b2ee","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4"},{"link_uuid":"62a3e9a4-e6e8-4f82-8fd0-06ccfbf2cd10","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"50b1-e181-3716-482c"},{"link_uuid":"0876874f-8d64-4057-a4f8-b4c4102f889e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f7da-baae-3c93-47e2"},{"link_uuid":"bcd65832-537f-4aab-b190-de6e9746526d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5334-3b4c-f626-4e12"},{"link_uuid":"3ffd54c8-60e1-43d3-953a-efa4293a2c69","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5984-5752-da66-48af"},{"link_uuid":"8dbf8ff5-320d-4c1d-a81d-74221d438763","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"edf7-946e-84be-48b3"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nA production `rebar create` call failed while committing a ticket event. The command reported the following output.\n\n```text\nError: git commit failed while holding lock: fatal: unable to write new index file\n```\n\nThe failure occurred in `/Users/joeoakhart/docs-epic-finish-20260823` while creating the F30B child of cepivorous-dynamitic-deer. Several ticket writes had succeeded in the same session. An exact-title search after the failure found no created ticket. The tracker then reported a clean status, no `.git/index.lock` existed, the filesystem had 458 GiB available with ample inodes, and an identical create call succeeded as peppery-dire-indianabat. The failed write therefore surfaced to the caller and required an operator retry.\n\n## Prior records\n\nlowcost-unsainted-wallaby records the same Git message when a test timer deletes the lock that Git owns during commit. Its accepted resolution states that production behavior was correct and intentionally excludes this message from retry classification. This occurrence came from a production CLI write and therefore is not resolved by that test-only correction. unheedful-custodial-bluebottle and interior-raspberry-titi cover different write-side filesystem messages. snide-cut-mussel covers `index.lock` contention and stale-lock reclamation.\n\n## Investigation Plan\n\n- Determine which process or recovery path can remove or invalidate the Git-owned index lock during a production ticket commit.\n- Reproduce the failure through the shared ticket-write seam with deterministic coordination instead of a timing sleep.\n- Decide whether the safe correction prevents the invalidation or retries the complete idempotent event commit after this exact failure.\n- Prove that recovery cannot duplicate an event, omit an event, or overwrite a concurrent ticket write.\n- Preserve bounded retry and actionable terminal diagnostics for persistent faults.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The production root cause is demonstrated with process and lock ownership evidence.\n- [x] A deterministic regression test reproduces the exact failure through a ticket-write entry point.\n- [x] One ticket-write invocation self-recovers from the transient occurrence or prevents the invalidation.\n- [x] Recovery commits exactly one intended event and preserves concurrent events.\n- [x] A persistent occurrence remains bounded and returns an actionable error.\n- [x] Focused store concurrency tests, lint, type checking, and the default test suite pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py","reason":"Add the pre-ref-update index-write signature to TRANSIENT_WRITE_MARKERS so the shared store retry self-heals it"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py","reason":"Regression: classification + add/commit self-heal + post-ref-update safety boundary"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py","reason":"Unit: the index-write signature classifies as TRANSIENT_FS"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","50b1-e181-3716-482c"],["relates_to","5334-3b4c-f626-4e12"],["relates_to","5984-5752-da66-48af"],["relates_to","f7da-baae-3c93-47e2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7ed755b1-fc42-4109-b2a9-f5b7daebe4fc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["tracker","concurrency","git"],"ticket_id":"553a-909b-5046-4494","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Production ticket write can fail with unable to write new index file","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6c4f2752-2105-4eb9-85df-e7d31d9b5b84","432afe07-df30-4da6-a897-1e6d025654c6","30ceb0bd-42a9-4ae6-9d68-043ac316d49b","2b157336-57c0-44de-b7bc-ac9275784959","bcd65832-537f-4aab-b190-de6e9746526d","3ffd54c8-60e1-43d3-953a-efa4293a2c69","7a89371b-eee6-4909-b02b-f8c79f6c64fb","7ed755b1-fc42-4109-b2a9-f5b7daebe4fc","8ea93ebb-095b-4cc4-88fa-c11825ca4fe9","8dbf8ff5-320d-4c1d-a81d-74221d438763","fa129565-b1c7-490d-ab1e-8f4086d7d9c7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787564359352339001,"uuid":"944f223d-16b6-47de-8280-96496013e649"}